WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.320
The report is eleven pages.

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.060
Her seniors would have preferred

3
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.240
eleven lines.

4
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.750
Or none.

5
00:00:07.289 --> 00:00:08.629
This is a made up case.

6
00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:11.349
Meera, a junior engineer,

7
00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:12.729
inspects a footbridge before

8
00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:14.609
Friday's opening, and finds

9
00:00:14.609 --> 00:00:16.439
cracks in two supports.

10
00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:18.255
Her seniors say:

11
00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:19.515
call it minor.

12
00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:21.275
The contractor would owe a

13
00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:22.915
penalty, and the ribbon is

14
00:00:22.915 --> 00:00:24.165
already ordered.

15
00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:25.695
The dilemma:

16
00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:28.435
does Meera sign off quietly, or

17
00:00:28.435 --> 00:00:30.265
put her concern on record?

18
00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:31.679
Option A:

19
00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:32.959
sign it off.

20
00:00:32.959 --> 00:00:34.339
Option B:

21
00:00:34.339 --> 00:00:35.679
post the photographs online

22
00:00:35.679 --> 00:00:38.179
tonight. Option C:

23
00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:39.459
send a written report up the

24
00:00:39.459 --> 00:00:40.919
chain, and to the vigilance

25
00:00:40.919 --> 00:00:43.889
officer. Pause here, and choose.

26
00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:46.379
Option A breaks the first two

27
00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.979
duties in Rule three:

28
00:00:47.979 --> 00:00:50.989
integrity, and devotion to duty.

29
00:00:51.494 --> 00:00:53.914
Option B has the right aim, and

30
00:00:53.914 --> 00:00:55.034
a risky route.

31
00:00:55.034 --> 00:00:56.674
It skips the channels that

32
00:00:56.674 --> 00:00:58.304
protect a complainant.

33
00:00:58.728 --> 00:01:00.828
Option C is the proper path.

34
00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:03.128
Since two thousand four, a

35
00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:04.488
government resolution lets

36
00:01:04.488 --> 00:01:06.288
complaints of misuse of office

37
00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:07.968
reach the Central Vigilance

38
00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.278
Commission, name kept private.

39
00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.950
A sound answer states the facts,

40
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.870
writes them down, uses the

41
00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.770
proper channel, and asks for

42
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.180
inspection first.

43
00:01:18.773 --> 00:01:19.833
Exam note:

44
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.533
the Whistle Blowers Act of

45
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:23.633
twenty fourteen has assent, but

46
00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:25.223
is not yet in force.

47
00:01:26.537 --> 00:01:27.364
For GS4:

48
00:01:27.364 --> 00:01:30.057
doing the right thing is a duty.

49
00:01:30.057 --> 00:01:31.987
Put it in writing.

50
00:01:33.011 --> 00:01:34.551
The ribbon cutting moves to next

51
00:01:34.551 --> 00:01:37.111
month. The bridge, as bridges

52
00:01:37.111 --> 00:01:39.081
prefer, stays up.
